-- title:
--   Unit principle on a crossing model after completion
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a Noetherian local domain, let $K$ be a field equipped with a $B$-algebra structure whose structure map $B \to K$ is injective, and let $W$ be a discrete valuation domain that is complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with $\pi \in W$ irreducible. Fix $E \ge 1$ and write $\mathcal{M} =$ `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E)` for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^{E}$, and `const (π ^ E) π` for the class of the constant series $\pi$. Assume given a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $B$ at its maximal ideal onto $\mathcal{M}$, an element $\varpi \in B$, an integer $k_0 \ge 1$ and a unit $w_0$ of $\mathcal{M}$ such that $\iota$ carries the image of $\varpi$ in the completion to $w_0 \cdot \mathrm{const}(\pi)^{k_0}$. Let $f \in K$ be nonzero, assume $f$ is a fraction of $B$ (there are $r_0, s_0 \in B$ with $s_0 \ne 0$ and $f \cdot r_0$-type relation $f\, s_0 = r_0$ in $K$), and assume that for every nonzero prime ideal $P$ of $B$ with $\varpi \notin P$ both $f$ and $f^{-1}$ lie in the image of the localisation $B_P$, i.e. each of them can be written as $r/s$ with $r, s \in B$, $s \notin P$, in the sense that $f\,s = r$ (respectively $f^{-1} s = r$) holds in $K$. Then there exist a unit $w$ of $\mathcal{M}$ and natural numbers $a, b, n, k$ with $a = 0$ or $b = 0$ such that for all $r, s \in B$ with $f\,s = r$ in $K$ one has, in $\mathcal{M}$, $$\iota(\hat r)\cdot \mathrm{const}(\pi)^{k} = \iota(\hat s)\cdot \bigl(w \cdot U(\pi^{E})^{a}\, V(\pi^{E})^{b}\, \mathrm{const}(\pi)^{n}\bigr),$$ where $\hat r, \hat s$ denote the images of $r, s$ in the completion and `U (π ^ E)`, `V (π ^ E)` are the two distinguished elements of $\mathcal{M}$. Informally: $f$ becomes the monomial $w\, U^{a}V^{b}\pi^{\,n-k}$ in the fraction field of the completion.
--
--   This is the generic form of the unit principle at a node: a fraction of $B$ which is invertible at every nonzero prime away from $\varpi$ becomes, after completion and identification with the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$, a unit times a monomial $U^{a}V^{b}\pi^{m}$ with $a=0$ or $b=0$, the integer $b-a$ being the slope. It feeds the analysis of functions and sections on the model of the modular curve at a supersingular point, being used by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_isUnit_and_read_eq_and_ord_placeOn_eq_zero_of_forall_ord_eq_zero_of_forall_isUnit_evalAt_of_chart_of_residue_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_isUnit_and_read_eq_and_ord_placeOn_eq_zero_of_forall_ord_eq_zero_of_forall_isUnit_evalAt_of_chart_of_residue_surjective) and [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_zpow_unit_principle_evalAt_read_chart_of_section_of_chart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_zpow_unit_principle_evalAt_read_chart_of_section_of_chart).
